<title>BELGIUM: Belgian BBL takes stake in Indian Bank.</title>
<headline>Belgian BBL takes stake in Indian Bank.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-09-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Belgian bank Banque Bruxelles Lambert said on Monday it struck a strategic cooperation accord with India's leading private bank Vysya Bank under which BBL will take a five percent stake in Vysya.</p>
<p>The deal, which still has to be vetted by the Bank of India, would also give BBL a seat on the board of directors.</p>
<p>BBL said the deal would allow it to improve its service to clients dealing with India.</p>
<p>Bangalore-based Vysya has 335 outlets and a capital-adequacy ratio of 11.9 percent.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
